### Configurações Globais de Ambiente
@host = http://localhost:3000/api

### 1. Criar Usuário Administrador (ADMIN)
# @no-log
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Carlos Administrador",
  "email": "admin@medclinic.com",
  "password": "SenhaSegura123",
  "role": "ADMIN"
}

###

### 2. Criar Usuário Atendente (ATTENDANT)
# @no-log
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mariana Atendente",
  "email": "mariana@medclinic.com",
  "password": "SenhaAtendente123",
  "role": "ATTENDANT"
}

###

### 3. Criar Usuário Padrão (Sem informar role - assume ATTENDANT)
# @no-log
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pedro Silva",
  "email": "pedro@medclinic.com",
  "password": "SenhaPedro123"
}

###

### 4.1 Realizar Login com o Administrador (Para capturar o Token)
# @no-log
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@medclinic.com",
  "password": "SenhaSegura123"
}

> {%
    // Este script guarda o token automaticamente no WebStorm após o login
    client.global.set("auth_token", response.body.token);
%}

###


### 4.2 Realizar Login com o Atendente (Para capturar o Token)
# @no-log
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mariana@medclinic.com",
  "password": "SenhaAtendente123"
}

> {%
    // Este script guarda o token automaticamente no WebStorm após o login
    client.global.set("auth_token", response.body.token);
%}

###

### 5. Testar Rota Protegida /me (Retorna dados do Usuário Atual)
# @no-log
GET {{host}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

###

### 6. Testar Rota Administrativa /admin/ping
# @no-log
GET {{host}}/admin/ping
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
